USER ARCHITECTURE.md
USER ````
USER # Address Book Web Application - Architecture Documentation
USER 
USER ## Section 1: Database Entity Mapping
USER 
USER | Field | Type | Constraints | Description |
USER |-------|------|-------------|-------------|
USER | `id` | Long | `@Id`, `@GeneratedValue`, non-null | Primary key, auto-increment |
USER | `firstName` | String | `@NotBlank`, max 50 chars | Contact first name |
USER | `lastName` | String | `@NotBlank`, max 50 chars | Contact last name |
USER | `email` | String | `@NotBlank`, `@Email`, max 100 chars | Contact email address |
USER | `phoneNumber` | String | `@NotBlank`, max 20 chars | Contact phone number |
USER | `address` | String | `@NotBlank`, max 255 chars | Physical address |
USER | `category` | String | `@NotBlank`, max 50 chars | Tag/Category (e.g., Family, Work) |
USER 
USER **Entity Location:** `src/main/java/com/addressbook/model/Contact.java`
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## Section 2: REST API Endpoints Specification
USER 
USER **Base Path:** `/api/contacts`
USER 
USER | HTTP Method | Endpoint | Request Body | Response Body | Description |
USER |-------------|----------|--------------|---------------|-------------|
USER | `GET` | `/api/contacts` | None | `[Contact]` (array) | List all contacts |
USER | `GET` | `/api/contacts/{id}` | None | `Contact` object | Get single contact by ID |
USER | `POST` | `/api/contacts` | `Contact` JSON | `Contact` object | Create new contact |
USER | `PUT` | `/api/contacts/{id}` | `Contact` JSON | `Contact` object | Update existing contact |
USER | `DELETE` | `/api/contacts/{id}` | None | `204 No Content` | Delete contact by ID |
USER | `GET` | `/api/contacts/search?q={query}` | None | `[Contact]` (array) | Search/filter by name or category |
USER 
USER ### POST Request/Response Example
USER 
USER **Request:**
USER ```json
USER POST /api/contacts
USER Content-Type: application/json
USER 
USER {
USER   "firstName": "John",
USER   "lastName": "Doe",
USER   "email": "john.doe@example.com",
USER   "phoneNumber": "+1-555-1234",
USER   "address": "123 Main Street, Anytown, USA",
USER   "category": "Family"
USER }
USER ```
USER 
USER **Response:**
USER ```json
USER HTTP/1.1 201 Created
USER Content-Type: application/json
USER 
USER {
USER   "id": 1,
USER   "firstName": "John",
USER   "lastName": "Doe",
USER   "email": "john.doe@example.com",
USER   "phoneNumber": "+1-555-1234",
USER   "address": "123 Main Street, Anytown, USA",
USER   "category": "Family"
USER }
USER ```
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## Section 3: Project Directory Layout
USER 
USER ```
USER address-book/
USER ├── pom.xml
USER ├── src/
USER │   ├── main/
USER │   │   ├── java/com/addressbook/
USER │   │   │   ├── AddressBookApplication.java
USER │   │   │   ├── config/DatabaseInitializer.java
USER │   │   │   ├── controller/ContactController.java
USER │   │   │   ├── model/Contact.java
USER │   │   │   ├── repository/ContactRepository.java
USER │   │   │   └── service/ContactService.java
USER │   │   └── resources/
USER │   │       ├── application.properties
USER │   │       ├── data.sql
USER │   │       └── static/ (index.html, css/, js/)
USER │   └── test/java/com/addressbook/
USER │       └── ContactControllerTest.java
USER └── ARCHITECTURE.md
USER ```
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## Section 4: Additional Notes
USER 
USER - **H2 Database Configuration:** In-memory or file-based configuration via `application.properties` for development and testing flexibility
USER - **Sample Data:** 5 sample contacts pre-populated in H2 database on startup via `data.sql` script
USER - **Validation:** Server-side validation using Spring `@Valid` annotations on controller method parameters with Bean Validation constraints
USER - **Frontend:** Vanilla JavaScript implementation using Fetch API for all CRUD operations, with client-side validation before API calls
USER ````
